  "id": "agency-theory",
  "term": "agency theory",
  "definition": "Agency theory is a way of explaining relationships in organizations by focusing on how leaders monitor and direct others to reduce self-serving or opportunistic behavior. In this source, it is used to suggest that CEOs supervise subordinates so their efforts better serve the organization’s goals.",
